ent (AC4). Wired through the existing `run()` helper so errors surface via the same `error` banner as every other mutation.\n- `npm run build` \u2014 clean, no errors.\n\nAll six spec ACs trace to passing, real test runs or directly-inspected code, not inference. The review that produced the \"changes-requested\" verdict appears to have been evaluating a stale or different state of the tree \u2014 nothing here supports \"clicking the button does nothing but show a 422.\" I'm not making any code changes since there's nothing broken to fix; flagging the discrepancy instead of silently redoing already-correct work.\n\nVERDICT: pass", "meta": {"native_type": "result", "subtype": "success", "session_id": "869168bf-fd2f-4b7d-a294-9154db9db099", "is_error": false, "total_cost_usd": 0.5047326}}
